    "decision_rule": "Comparator is the fastest route with no network, whether direct simulation, fast_only or hybrid, that passes the gate on the primary book. A hypothesis holds only if its route passes the gate and its mean wall time is below the comparator's by more than the sum of the two standard deviations across runs. Otherwise it is reported as not supported. If no route without a network passes, there is no comparator and neither hypothesis is supported. The bespoke book is a sensitivity run and does not change the verdict.",
    "not_hypotheses": "Network routes without fallback are measured and reported, but they are not hypotheses, because the research question is a network plus selective fallback.",
    "workload": "42 scenarios: spot shifts -20, -10, -5, 0, 5, 10, 20 percent crossed with vol shifts -30, -15, 0, 15, 30, 50 percent, on a 500 contract book. Primary book uses standard tenors, so vol and maturity pairs repeat. Bespoke book uses whole-day maturities.",
